          "code": "PREPARE_DATA_FOR_DISPLAY_AGENT",
          "id": "1765229900132",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Display the opportunities as a list\nFor each opportunity, display a badge that indicates how well it matches the applicant's profile.\n\nMap badge colors based on the match score as follows:\n- Match score 85 and above → Green Badge (\"Excellent Match\")\n- Match score between 70-84 → Blue Badge (\"Very Good Match\")\n- Match score between 55-69 → Yellow Badge (\"Good Match\")\n- Match score between 40-54 → Orange Badge (\"Moderate Match\")\n- Match score below 40 → Red Badge (\"Fair Match\")\n\nDo NOT use emojis, warning symbols, or stars. Only use the badge to show match status, based on the match score."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Display LLM Agent Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_LLM_AGENT",
          "id": "1765229991674",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765229991679_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Here is my internal opportunity data (note internal opportunities, match scores, skill alignment, and how they match my profile and career goals):\n{{$context.$variables.matchedOpportunities}}\n\nHere are the candidate's skills and profile data (use only if necessary):\n{{$context.$variables.candidateProfile}}\n\nTASK:\nGenerate a messageListWidget showing the top internal opportunities relevant to the applicant.\n\nDISPLAY RULES:\n- Show ONLY a messageListWidget.\n- Limit to top 5 opportunities sorted by highest match quality.\n- Each item must include title, summary, badgeText, priority, timestamp, and additionalAction.\n- Do NOT include actual timestamps.\n\nTITLE:\n- Use a concise, descriptive title summarizing the nature of the opportunities.\n\nITEM STRUCTURE:\n- Title: Job or Gig title with a brief role descriptor.\n- Subtitle: Do not display OpportunityType here.\n- Summary: Explain relevance using the match score, skill alignment, experience fit, and career growth. When mentioning skills, always format them in Title Case with each word capitalized.\n\nOPPORTUNITY TYPE PLACEMENT:\n- Display OpportunityType (\"Job\" or \"Gig\") in the timestamp position.\n- Do NOT display any actual timestamp.\n\nBADGE RULES:\n- Use badgeText for the match label.\n- Use priority for badge severity.\n- Match score 85 or above: badgeText \"Excellent match\", priority \"success\".\n- Match score 70-84: badgeText \"Very good match\", priority \"medium\".\n- Match score 55-69: badgeText \"Good match\", priority \"warning\".\n- Match score 40-54: badgeText \"Moderate match\", priority \"alert\".\n- Match score below 40: badgeText \"Fair match\", priority \"alert\".\n\nACTION RULES:\n- Every item must show a visible widget-level button using additionalAction.\n- Set additionalAction.text to \"View Details\".\n- Set additionalAction.command to the matching ora.Invoke command below.\n- Also set the item action field to the same command so row click and button click both work.\n- Do not use additionalActions, actions, link, or any unsupported action field.\n\nFor Job opportunities, use this command format exactly:\nora.Invoke(\"VIEWOPPORTUNITYDETAILS\", {\"JobNumber\":\"<JobNumber>\",\"OpportunityType\":\"Job\",\"Title\":\"<Title>\",\"Score\":\"<MatchScore>\"})\n\nFor Gig opportunities, use this command format exactly:\nora.Invoke(\"VIEWOPPORTUNITYDETAILS\", {\"GigId\":\"<GigId>\",\"OpportunityType\":\"Gig\",\"Title\":\"<Title>\",\"Score\":\"<MatchScore>\"})\n\nUse the existing app action code VIEWOPPORTUNITYDETAILS exactly.\nDo not ask clarifying questions.\nReturn only a valid messageListWidget JSON.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
